LIMITATIONS:
MATCH observes declared inputs, not all transitive dependencies or external services.
Before/after snapshots do not detect temporary changes restored between observations.
Local same-user tampering is not prevented by integrity hashes. Raw output/argv may contain
secrets. Windows inherits directory ACL; shared overrides are not promised private.
Output >=64 MiB is incomplete. Descendant-held pipe wait is bounded; killing the entire
descendant tree is not promised. Other OSes unverified. No automatic pruning.
Code coverage percentage was not measured; no claim of 100% branch coverage is made.

